ue "CCS"} "Cross Country Skiing"] "\n" [:option {:value "FSK"} "Figure Skating"] "\n" [:option {:value "IHO"} "Ice Hockey"] "\n" [:option {:value "NCB"} "Nordic Combined"] "\n" [:option {:value "SJP"} "Ski Jumping"]]] [:script {} "$('#sports_in_same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/34/sports/'+$('#sports_in_same_games_select').val()})"] [:form {:id "other_games_form", :class "form-inline", :style "display: inline", :method "get"} [:select {:name "year", :id "sport_in_other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "Speed Skating in other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "29"} "1924 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "30"} "1928 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "31"} "1932 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "32"} "1936 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "33"} "1948 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "35"} "1956 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "36"} "1960 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "37"} "1964 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "38"} "1968 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "39"} "1972 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "40"} "1976 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "41"} "1980 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "42"} "1984 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "43"} "1988 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "44"} "1992 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "45"} "1994 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "46"} "1998 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "47"} "2002 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "49"} "2006 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "57"} "2010 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "66"} "2012 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "58"} "2014 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "68"} "2016 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "60"} "2018 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "70"} "2020 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "62"} "2022 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "73"} "2024 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "72"} "2026 Winter Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/SSK'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Speed Skating at the 1952 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "16 – 19 February 1952"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "4"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/93"} "Bislett Stadion, Oslo"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "With the 1952 edition, the Winter Olympics first came to Scandinavia. The competitions proved very popular with the public, which was also the case for the speed skating events. Held at " [:a {:href "/venues/93"} "Bislett Stadium"] ", there was room for 29,000 spectators, much more than at previous Olympics."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The first rink at Bislett was opened on 1908, but it was closed for relocation and renovation in 1916. After its reopening in 1922, it was Oslo’s secondary skating rink (behind Frogner), although it hosted the 1925 World Championships, as well as various international socialist championships. After the war, it took over from Frogner and hosted the 1947 and 1949 World Championships before being used in the Olympics. Until the early 1980s, it was one of the world’s premier skating rinks, but it lost that status when it was decided it would no longer be used for skating in 1988. Since the 1960s, the stadium (now renovated) is in use for the annual Bislett Games, one of the world’s foremost track and field meets."] "\n\n" [:p {} "All countries participating in the Oslo speed skating events had competed at earlier Games, with Germany and Japan returning after their exclusion in " [:a {:href "/editions/33/sports/SSK"} "1948"] ". Germany was only represented by West German athletes, including their sole skater, " [:a {:href "/athletes/95342"} "Theo Meding"] ". Still missing was the Soviet Union, which would make its Olympic début later in the year in " [:a {:href "/editions/13"} "Helsinki"] ". The Soviet male skaters improved record after record on the highland rink at Medeo, although these times were approached with suspicion, since the skaters did not compete internationally. Remarkably, the Soviet female skaters did appear at World Championships, which they dominated. Women’s skating, however, was still not on the programme in Oslo."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The speed skating part of these Olympics was dominated by home favorite " [:a {:href "/athletes/83598"} "Hjalmar Andersen"] ". He had won all major all-round titles in 1950, 1951, and 1952, and would win three gold medals. Behind him, Dutch skaters won their country’s first Olympic speed skating medals."] "\n\n" [:p {} "An important absentee in Oslo was Hungarian-born " [:a {:href "/athletes/96146"} "Kornél Pajor"] ". He had placed third at the European Championships two weeks before the Olympics and, in 1949, he had won the World Championships at Bislett, winning both long distances. However, after that title, Pajor did not return to communist Hungary and defected to Sweden. After initially competing as stateless, Pajor represented Sweden in 1952. Because of his change of nationality so briefly before the Olympics, Pajor was not allowed to compete in Oslo."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/997"} "500 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "16 February 1952"] "\n" [:td {} "41"] "\n" [:td {} "14"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/998"} "1,500 metres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "18 February 1952"] "\n" [:td {} "39"] "\n" [:td {} "13"] "\n"